// The class of each of clang's options in a normalized command
// (classify_option):
//
//   OPTION_GROUP(GROUP, CLASS)   every option of clang's option group GROUP
//   OPTION(ID, CLASS)            the option ID
//
// CLASS is an ArgClass, or LeftOut for an option the command leaves out.
// The lines apply in order, a later one over an earlier one, over what
// clang's tables say first: what the driver ignores and what cc1 keeps in
// its CodeGenOptions are left out, the rest is Semantic. A command keeps
// only what clice's analysis reads: what predefines macros, answers
// __has_feature and its kin, sets the language or the target, finds the
// headers, decides the diagnostics shown, or names the precompiled files
// clice builds itself.

// The input, unknown arguments and `--`, which a command reads apart.
OPTION(INPUT, LeftOut)
OPTION(UNKNOWN, LeftOut)
OPTION(_DASH_DASH, LeftOut)

// Debug information: in a C file without unwind tables on an ELF or Mach-O
// target (Kbuild's), whether it is on decides __GCC_HAVE_DWARF2_CFI_ASM.
OPTION_GROUP(DebugInfo_Group, Semantic)

// ...but not what cc1 makes of it, which only code generation reads.
OPTION(debug_info_kind_EQ, LeftOut)

// The warnings and errors the user sees.
OPTION_GROUP(Diag_Group, Diagnostics)
OPTION_GROUP(pedantic_Group, Diagnostics)
OPTION(w, Diagnostics)

